# The file areas of the BBS. One area per line, in menu order:
#
#   slug|Title|Short text
#
# The slug is what a file's .meta remembers: a-z, 0-9 and dashes, at most 20 characters.
# Do not change the slug of an area that has files; change its title instead.
# The first area is the default: scp -O uploads land there, and so does anything without
# a known area.
#
# To add an area, add a line. To remove one, remove its line: no file is deleted, its files
# show under the default area, and putting the line back returns them to where they were.
# It takes effect at once, with no restart.
general|General|Anything that fits nowhere else
demos|Demos|Demos, intros and cracktros
music|Music|Modules, tunes and samples
utilities|Utilities|Tools and useful programs
